// A process call whose argument has to reach the callee's conditional and the
// callee's embedded restriction.
//
// Inlining a call substitutes the actual arguments for the formal parameters
// over the whole definition body
// (Theory/Text/Parser/Sapic.hs:293-312, through
// Theory/Sapic/Process.hs:392-408#applyM).  The formula argument of
// `mapTermsAction` reaches an embedded `_restrict`
// (Theory/Sapic/Process.hs:155) and the one of `mapTermsComb` reaches an `if`
// condition (Theory/Sapic/Process.hs:165), so `P(z)` puts `z` inside both.
//
// The conditional's rules therefore read `process="if Eq( z.1, 'a' )"` and are
// named `ifEqza_0_11` and `ifEqza_1_11` after that string
// (Sapic/Facts.hs:401#stripNonAlphanumerical), and the embedded restriction's
// rule carries `_restrict( Q( w.1 ) )` over the `in`'s own variable.
//
// Mode `match`: the two engines agree on this shape.  No corpus theory calls a
// definition whose body starts with a conditional, and no process under
// tamarin-prover/examples carries an embedded `_restrict` at all, so no gate
// row covers either substitution.
//
// Compared slices: the wf report block, which pins the run clean, AND the
// `theory … end` echo, which carries the `process=` attribute of the rules and
// the names derived from it.

theory SapicCallCond
begin

predicates: Eq(a, b) <=> a = b
          , Q(a) <=> a = a

let P(y) = if Eq(y, 'a') then out('yes') else out('no')

let R(v) = [ ] --[ Ev(v), _restrict( Q(v) ) ]-> [ ]; out('done')

process:
  ( ( in(z); P(z) )
  | ( in(w); R(w) ) )

end
